{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/503547-needing-for-some-opinions-on-my-adventure-aberrant-game","id":503547,"title":"Needing for some opinions on my Adventure-Aberrant game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-04T15:24:10-07:00","id":503547,"title":"Needing for some opinions on my Adventure-Aberrant game","content":"Warning: i bend the rules and the metaplot..A Lot.<br /> <br /> for an entire year i ran a game of adventure that went through time, the characters passed away due aging but they were witness to the galatea.<br /> The catch was that during the 1940's they discovered a Man who was pulling the strings all along, a super scientist who was a lab rat to Primoris. a human with an intelligence utterly high and with a lot of 'Curiosity'.<br /> He was known as The Spectre and he was one of the main triggers behind the Galatea (working with Divis Mal so he could get his payback eventually).<br /> on one swift strike he managed to kill about the 80% of the Metahuman population (using one of the scenarios, soon after ibiza) and killing Divis Mal.<br /> his effects on the world were so big that well...lets say that i read a lot of comics and i went a bit of Days of the Future Past on the plot (with machines hunting down aberrants and killing them, and slowly going Skynet on humans as well).<br /> the players soon found out that The Spectre had survive the nuclear attacks and that he actually Won.<br /> <br /> So, the surviving players decided to go back to the 1940's and try to kill that ..Thing, once it for all.<br /> Now, joining up forces with their old Adventure characters and old villians (i pretty much took all the villians from Hellboy during the 1940s), they must face The Spectre once more..not knowing that he is not Taking his time anymore, and breaking the timelines once it for all in order to Win (that, and capturing Novas, experimenting with them and create aberrants before the galatea)<br /> <br /> <br /> Any ideas, suggestions?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:56:35-07:00","id":503865,"title":"","content":"Hello Crowley.<br /> We don't all have to play the exact same game, but it can be confusing to hear someone who has clearly played it so differently asking for advice - when no-one but they know what is really going on.<br /> As with your other thread inquiring about this peculiar intersection, you may need to be more specific. What is the end game plan for this 'Spectre'? It seems like the character is wiping out all novas to slowly hunt down and kill all humans - what exactly does Spectre gain from this? What drives him to this end?<br /> I can assume that his primary power-set is one of stealth, judging by the name and his power to remain hidden even right beneath Dr Primoris' nose - he's a lab rat and plays to mastermind tropes, so we might assume mega-mental. But i'm not certain i'm really following what you want.<br /> Are you looking for suggestions on where to take the character arc of this 'Spectre' or where to take the game (adventures, setting, PC arcs, etc...) itself?<br /> Please forgive me if i'm unclear, i'm happy to clarify if needed. Your english is much better than my spanish could ever hope to be at this point.<br /> -smile-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-09T20:48:44-07:00","id":509533,"title":"","content":"mainly, the idea of jumping from aberrant to an adventure campain.<br /> <br /> As the spectre, he is a high mental character, same with stealth and advanced contacts. His plan is purely based on the idea of Psychohistory (Isaac Asimov), he is a sociopath who is curious about the constant &quot;What if&quot; scenarios and creating them so he can tell how predictable humanity is.<br /> <br /> basically, he is a big boy with out sense of morale or ethics with the biggest ant farm ever and with unlimited resources to experiment with them. He doesnt care about his own self preservation, and as for his other stats, he is completely human.<br /> <br /> the question is, how feaseble is for a guy like this to exist within the aberrant universe, and the whole idea of time travel and cross over with Adventure. as well a guy who managed to kill pretty much every nova","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-11T05:55:10-07:00","id":510567,"title":"","content":"The path of getting from Aberrant in 2008 to Adventure! in 1922 almost inevitably requires time travel to work. Unless you want to bring Process 418 forward 114 years, as a 'new' Adventure! period.<br /> I'm hoping you are gunning for 'monolithic evil' with the Spectre, because i'm yet to see any other possible use for the character - i'm guessing you are setting this big-bad up for a huge toppling by the PCs in the future. I'm not sure what his apocalypse has to do with Asimov's Psychohistory, because resisting the societal changes of N-day and falling into a repressive Skynet-like pogrom against humanity in general is a slap in the face to; and ultimately the end of Psychohistory. Psychohistory is about the path of least resistance and is used as a tool of survival. Also, if he displays sociopathic, narcissist characteristics, then how is self-preservation not important to him? He would think: &quot;What is the point of anything when the Spectre isn't the centre of it?&quot;.<br /> Death isn't anything that any narcissist goes gently into. But, the Spectre, from what you've shared seems more like a fanatic of some variety.<br /> Why does he need a measure of how predictable Humanity is? What is the next step here? Endless 'what ifs' make for a flimsy kind of endgame for such a sledgehammer climax (luring and killing all novas with nukes, i gather), i am willing to accept the idea that he, like Mal, is completely bugging out with isolation after the interim years and just becomes irreconcilably alien. But even then, it seems like driving the earth, and by extension himself, extinct is never something to be worked so hard towards.<br /> Since i still don't understand the Spectre's motivations, maybe you can sketch out the differences between the Adventure! material as it's printed and how you will be running it. You've already mentioned that Spectre worked with Primoris, so can i assume the rest of the era is mostly intact from the book? Will the group be interacting with the Aeon society in the past, if it's still used in your game? Apologies for all the questions, but i need to get a sense of what you're doing before i can suggest anything helpful to do in the same vein","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4458-nihilist","name":"Nihilist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4458_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}